// The `core/hash` conformance package.
//
// Four algorithms, each pinned to the vectors its publisher wrote down rather
// than to whatever this implementation happened to answer the first time it
// ran: FNV-1a's reference vectors, the CRC-32C check value together with RFC
// 3720 B.4's three iSCSI cases, and the SipHash-2-4 reference implementation's
// table. An agreement with a published number is a claim two implementations
// can be compared on; an agreement with a recorded output is a claim about
// nothing.
//
// It is also a hard test of the *language*: U32 and U64 wrapping arithmetic,
// exclusive-or, both shifts, rotation built from two of them, tail recursion
// over an eight-octet word, and the same answers on a backend where a U64 is a
// machine word and on one where it is a BigInt.
